    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Asthma:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " cornerstone of therapy, for long-term control of inflammation and symptoms. Preferred reliever at every step is a low-dose ICS–beta-agonist combination (as needed for mild asthma; maintenance + reliever for moderate–severe persistent)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Adult starting doses (no prior ICS):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " fluticasone furoate 100 mcg once daily (max 200 mcg); beclomethasone 40–80 mcg twice daily (max 320 mcg twice daily); budesonide DPI 360 mcg twice daily (max 720 mcg twice daily); mometasone HFA 100 mcg 2 inhalations twice daily (max 800 mcg/day); ciclesonide 80 mcg twice daily if on bronchodilators alone (max 160 mcg twice daily). Once stable, titrate to the lowest effective dose."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Contraindicated as primary treatment of status asthmaticus or acute asthma needing intensive measures. Caution: can worsen TB, fungal, bacterial, viral, parasitic or ocular HSV infection; chickenpox/measles can be severe or fatal in non-immune patients. Switching from oral steroids: risk of adrenal insufficiency, taper the systemic steroid slowly."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Fluticasone is a CYP3A4 substrate:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (eg, ketoconazole) raise exposure; use caution."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Check BMD at baseline and periodically; monitor growth in children; consider ophthalmology referral with ocular symptoms or long-term use."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Acute overdose rarely needs more than observation; chronic overdose can cause hypercorticism."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
